  "comments": "There is some uncertainty about the 1914/3 overdate variety, as some claim it might have been caused by a damaged die.<br /><br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5d7790dddc534.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5d7790dddc534.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br /><br />\r\nAccording to the legend, the bison used as a model for this coin was &quot;Black Diamond&quot; (1893-1915), a famous bison at the Central Park zoo in New York City.<br />\r\nIf there is a mintmark, it is below E C of FIVE CENTS.<br /><br />\r\n1914<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/637fa73be77c5.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/637fa73be77c5.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br />\r\n1916<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/637fa774035a5.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/637fa774035a5.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br />\r\n1918<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/637fa78fee480.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/637fa78fee480.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br />\r\n1934<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/637fa7acc6b59.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/637fa7acc6b59.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br />\r\n1935<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/637fa7c557b5b.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/637fa7c557b5b.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br />\r\n1936<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/637fa7d2e5130.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/637fa7d2e5130.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br />\r\n1937<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/637fa7dfb92